    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0689" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg629"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Uhl</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note, No. 108, of
                    the 24th instant, asking to be made acquainted with the names of the British
                    vessels, with their officers, composing the Bering Sea patrolling fleet for this
                    season, I have the honor to inform you that Her Majesty’s ships <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nymphe</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Pheasant</hi>
                    are under orders to proceed to Bering Sea for patrol duty.</p>
                <p>I inclose a list of the officers now holding appointments on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nymphe</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Pheasant.</hi></p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian Pauncefote</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d567-a1.xml" xpointer="d567-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
